(14, 1, 554, 3, 7, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"simple\",\"grounded_question_id\":3,\"grade\":\"Year 1\",\"topic\":\"Counting and number bonds\"}', 'After 7, the next counting number is 8.', NULL, '2026-06-19 20:41:07'),
(15, 1, 554, 24, 7, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"simple\",\"grounded_question_id\":24,\"grade\":\"Year 1\",\"topic\":\"Counting and number bonds\"}', 'When we count, we say numbers in order. Let\'s count: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7... The very next number we say is 8! So, 8 comes after 7.', NULL, '2026-06-19 20:41:33'),
(16, 1, 554, 24, 7, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"common_mistake\",\"grounded_question_id\":24,\"grade\":\"Year 1\",\"topic\":\"Counting and number bonds\"}', 'After 7, the next counting number is 8.', NULL, '2026-06-19 20:41:56'),
(17, 1, 554, 24, 7, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"hint\",\"grounded_question_id\":24,\"grade\":\"Year 1\",\"topic\":\"Counting and number bonds\"}', 'After 7, the next counting number is 8.', NULL, '2026-06-19 20:42:22'),
(18, 1, 573, 36, 13, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"simple\",\"grounded_question_id\":36,\"grade\":\"Year 1\",\"topic\":\"Agricultural Economics and Far Business\"}', 'Farmers sell the food they grow so they can get money. This money helps them buy new seeds for their farm and things for their family, like food and clothes.', NULL, '2026-06-20 16:24:10'),
(19, 1, 573, 36, 13, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"similar_example\",\"grounded_question_id\":36,\"grade\":\"Year 1\",\"topic\":\"Agricultural Economics and Far Business\"}', 'Imagine you make a yummy cake. If you sell your cake, you get money. You can then use that money to buy new ingredients for another cake or a toy you really want! Farmers do something similar. They sell the food they grow to get money so they can buy things like new seeds for their farm or clothes for their family.', NULL, '2026-06-20 16:24:33'),
(20, 1, 573, 38, 13, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"hint\",\"grounded_question_id\":38,\"grade\":\"Year 1\",\"topic\":\"Agricultural Economics and Far Business\"}', 'Think about who often lives and works together on a farm.', NULL, '2026-06-20 16:32:36'),
(21, 1, 573, 38, 13, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"similar_example\",\"grounded_question_id\":38,\"grade\":\"Year 1\",\"topic\":\"Agricultural Economics and Far Business\"}', 'Imagine your family has a big garden. Everyone helps out, right? Maybe your brother helps water the plants, and your sister helps pick the yummy vegetables. A farm is like a super big garden, and the farmer\'s family helps with all the important jobs, like putting seeds in the ground or giving food to the animals.', NULL, '2026-06-20 16:32:59'),
(22, 1, 573, 38, 13, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"similar_example\",\"grounded_question_id\":38,\"grade\":\"Year 1\",\"topic\":\"Agricultural Economics and Far Business\"}', 'Imagine you have a big garden at home. Sometimes your mom, dad, or even your big brother or sister might help you water the plants or pick the yummy tomatoes, right? It\'s kind of like that on a farm! Farmers often have their family members, like their children or cousins, help them with all the important jobs, like feeding the animals or gathering the eggs.', NULL, '2026-06-20 16:41:07'),
(23, 1, 573, 37, 13, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"simple\",\"grounded_question_id\":37,\"grade\":\"Year 1\",\"topic\":\"Agricultural Economics and Far Business\"}', 'Farmers need to buy seeds to plant new crops. They also buy food for their animals, tools to help them work, and fuel for their tractors.', NULL, '2026-06-20 16:47:15'),
(24, 1, 573, 35, 14, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"simple\",\"grounded_question_id\":35,\"grade\":\"Year 1\",\"topic\":\"Agricultural Economics and Far Business\"}', 'Hello! Farmers grow yummy things in their fields. They grow vegetables like carrots, fruits like apples, and grains like wheat. They sell these so we can eat them! So, C is the right answer.', 'flagged', '2026-06-21 06:06:26'),
(25, 1, 573, 37, 14, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"simple\",\"grounded_question_id\":37,\"grade\":\"Year 1\",\"topic\":\"Agricultural Economics and Far Business\"}', 'Farmers buy tiny seeds to grow yummy food. They also buy food for their animals, helpful tools, and special gas for their big tractors.', NULL, '2026-06-21 06:08:12'),
(26, 1, 573, 37, 14, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"similar_example\",\"grounded_question_id\":37,\"grade\":\"Year 1\",\"topic\":\"Agricultural Economics and Far Business\"}', 'You want a similar example! That\'s a super way to learn. Think about when you need new pencils for drawing. A farmer also needs to buy new things for their farm to do their work. For example, if a farmer wants to grow juicy tomatoes, they need to buy tomato seeds. This is just like buying seeds for new crops. Or, if their tractor needs to drive, they need to buy fuel, just like a car needs petrol!', NULL, '2026-06-21 06:08:29'),
(27, 1, 573, 39, 14, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"step_by_step\",\"grounded_question_id\":39,\"grade\":\"Year 1\",\"topic\":\"Agricultural Economics and Far Business\"}', 'You got it right! A farm business is all about making choices. First, farmers choose what plants to grow, like corn or strawberries. Then, they choose which animals to raise, like cows or chickens. After that, they decide how to sell their food to earn money. It\'s just like running a little food shop!', NULL, '2026-06-21 06:09:51'),
(28, 1, 620, 46, 15, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"simple\",\"grounded_question_id\":46,\"grade\":\"Year 3\",\"topic\":\"Year 3 Computer Studies Syllabus\"}', 'It\'s super smart to think about how to use a computer mouse safely! It helps your hand and wrist stay happy and healthy, so they don\'t get tired or sore. Here are two important rules: 1. Try to keep your wrist straight, like a ruler, not bent up or down. This helps your hand feel comfy. 2. Hold the mouse gently, like you\'re holding a little bird. Don\'t squeeze it too hard! This keeps your fingers relaxed. Following these rules helps you use the computer for a long time without your hand feeling yucky!', NULL, '2026-06-21 08:10:46'),
(29, 1, 620, 55, 16, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"simple\",\"grounded_question_id\":55,\"grade\":\"Year 3\",\"topic\":\"Year 3 Geography Syllabus\"}', 'You did a great job thinking about directions! This question wants us to use words like \'right\' and \'behind\' to find the window. If the teacher\'s desk is on your right, and the window is behind the desk, then the window is behind you and on your right side. We use these words to explain where things are from where you are standing.', NULL, '2026-06-21 20:48:49'),
(30, 1, 620, 72, 18, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"hint\",\"grounded_question_id\":72,\"grade\":\"Year 3\",\"topic\":\"Year 3 Science Syllabus\"}', 'The Earth\'s rotation causes different parts of the planet to face the sun, resulting in day and night. This rotation leads to distinct observable features in the sky, such as the presence of the sun and brightness during the day, and the moon and stars against a dark sky at night.', NULL, '2026-06-21 22:19:39'),
(31, 1, 620, 72, 18, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"simple\",\"grounded_question_id\":72,\"grade\":\"Year 3\",\"topic\":\"Year 3 Science Syllabus\"}', 'You\'re off to a super start! You correctly mentioned the sun and clouds for the daytime sky. To show a difference, we need to think about what we see at night too! For example, during the day, the sky is bright and we see the sun. But at night, the sky is dark and we don\'t see the sun. Another difference is that during the day we often see clouds, but at night we can often see the moon and twinkling stars!', NULL, '2026-06-21 22:19:56'),
(32, 1, 620, 79, 25, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"similar_example\",\"grounded_question_id\":79,\"grade\":\"Year 3\",\"topic\":\"Year 3 Mathematics Syllabus\"}', 'To order numbers, compare their hundreds digit first. 152 has 1 hundred, 215 has 2 hundreds, and 512 has 5 hundreds. So, 152 is the smallest, followed by 215, and then 512.', NULL, '2026-06-22 06:29:19'),
(33, 1, 620, 70, 31, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"simple\",\"grounded_question_id\":70,\"grade\":\"Year 3\",\"topic\":\"Year 3 Science Syllabus\"}', 'When a scientist does an experiment, they want to find out what makes something happen. For part a), the scientist is changing only one thing: the type of soil. This is because she wants to see if different soils make plants grow differently. For part b), to make sure her test is fair, she keeps other things the same, like giving the plants the same amount of water and putting them in the same sunny spot. For part c), it\'s super important to keep other things the same! If she changed too many things at once, she wouldn\'t know if the soil made the plant grow tall, or if it was something else, like more water. Keeping things the same helps her find the real reason for any changes she sees. You\'re doing great thinking about how scientists work!', NULL, '2026-06-24 07:55:26'),
(34, 1, 620, 46, 32, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"simple\",\"grounded_question_id\":46,\"grade\":\"Year 3\",\"topic\":\"Year 3 Computer Studies Syllabus\"}', 'Hi there! It\'s really smart to think about how to use your computer mouse safely. This helps your hand and wrist stay happy and healthy, so you can keep playing and learning! Here are two important rules: 1. Try to keep your wrist straight, like a flat road, not bent up or down. This helps your hand feel comfy. 2. Hold the mouse gently, like you\'re holding a feather. Don\'t squeeze it too hard! A light touch is much better for your hand. Great job thinking about how to be safe with computers!', NULL, '2026-06-25 14:52:53'),
(35, 1, 622, 73, 33, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"simple\",\"grounded_question_id\":73,\"grade\":\"Year 3\",\"topic\":\"Year 3 Science Syllabus\"}', 'A scientific question needs to be testable and specific. When observing and recording, it\'s important to have a clear method for measurement and a structured way to document the results, such as a table, to make comparisons easy and reliable.', NULL, '2026-06-25 15:00:40'),
(36, 1, 622, 49, 34, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"simple\",\"grounded_question_id\":49,\"grade\":\"Year 3\",\"topic\":\"Year 3 Computer Studies Syllabus\"}', 'You did really well with opening the program! Clicking the Start button and finding the program are perfect steps. When you want to close it, clicking the \'X\' button is exactly right. Sometimes, after you click \'X\', the computer asks if you want to save your picture. It\'s good to remember to choose to save or not before the program closes completely.', NULL, '2026-06-25 15:08:13'),
(37, 1, 622, 49, 34, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"step_by_step\",\"grounded_question_id\":49,\"grade\":\"Year 3\",\"topic\":\"Year 3 Computer Studies Syllabus\"}', 'Knowing how to open and close programs is a fundamental skill for using a computer. These steps are common across many applications and operating systems.', NULL, '2026-06-25 15:08:20'),
(38, 3, 682, 83, 61, 'gemini-2.5-flash', '{\"mode\":\"simple\",\"grounded_question_id\":83,\"grade\":\"Year 1\",\"topic\":\"Agriculture and the Environment\"}', 'It\'s super important to keep our rivers and wells clean! One easy way is to never throw rubbish, like sweet wrappers or old toys, into the water. Also, we can make sure dirty water from washing hands or clothes doesn\'t go straight into the river. Doing these things helps keep the water safe for everyone!', NULL, '2026-07-02 09:19:12');
