(124, 33, 71, 1, 'weak_topic', 'B', 1, 1.00, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-25 14:56:58', '2026-06-25 14:56:03', '2026-06-25 14:56:58'),
(125, 33, 72, 2, 'weak_topic', 'During the daytime, the Sun is the primary object, casting immense brightness and warmth. In contrast, the night sky reveals thousands of distant stars and frequently the Moon.', 1, 2.00, NULL, 'That\'s a fantastic description! You clearly explained two key differences between the day and night sky.', '2026-06-25 14:58:03', '2026-06-25 14:56:03', '2026-06-25 14:58:03'),
(126, 33, 70, 3, 'weak_topic', 'a) What is the one thing the scientist is changing?The type of soil (sandy, clay, and loam).b) List two things the scientist is keeping the same.(Choose any two from the list below)The amount of water given every day.The sunny spot where the pots are kept (amount of light/temperature).The type of seed used (three identical seeds).The size or type of pot.c) Why is it important to keep other things the same?To make sure it is a fair test.This ensures that any difference in plant height is only caused by the soil, and not by something else like water or sunlight.', 1, 4.00, NULL, 'Excellent work! You\'ve clearly explained all the key aspects of a fair test in this investigation.', '2026-06-25 14:58:49', '2026-06-25 14:56:03', '2026-06-25 14:58:49'),
(127, 33, 73, 4, 'weak_topic', 'a) Write one scientific question you could ask about this.Which type of paper towel absorbs the most water?(Alternative: \"Does Paper Towel A absorb more water than Paper Towel B?\")b) Describe how you would observe and record your findings.How to observe (what to look for):Measure the left-over water: Pour equal amounts of water onto two plates. Place one paper towel on each plate. Lift them up and look at how much water is left on each plate. The plate with the least water shows the most absorbent towel.Count the drops: Dip each towel into water and count how many drops drip out when you squeeze them.', 0, 2.00, 'partial_answer', 'Your scientific question is excellent! For describing how to observe and record, you\'ve given good ideas for what to look for. To make it even better, explain how you would measure the water accurately and record your results, perhaps in a table.', '2026-06-25 14:59:50', '2026-06-25 14:56:03', '2026-06-25 14:59:50'),
(128, 33, 74, 5, 'spaced_review', 'B', 1, 1.00, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-25 14:59:31', '2026-06-25 14:56:03', '2026-06-25 14:59:31'),
(129, 34, 46, 1, 'weak_topic', '1. Keep your wrist straightDo not bend your wrist up, down, or sideways while holding the mouse.Keep your hand, wrist, and forearm in a straight, level line to avoid strain.2. Hold the mouse with a loose, relaxed gripDo not squeeze or grip the mouse too tightly.Rest your hand gently on top of the mouse and use your whole arm to move it, rather than just twisting your wrist.', 1, 4.00, NULL, 'Excellent! You\'ve clearly described two key rules for safe mouse use, which will help prevent discomfort and injury.', '2026-06-25 15:04:59', '2026-06-25 15:03:53', '2026-06-25 15:04:59'),
(130, 34, 45, 2, 'weak_topic', '1. Monitor (or Screen)Function: It displays visual information, pictures, text, and videos so you can see what you are doing on the computer.2. Central Processing Unit (CPU)Function: It acts as the \"brain\" of the computer. It processes data, runs programs, and tells all the other parts what to do.', 1, 4.00, NULL, 'Excellent work! You have correctly identified two main parts of a computer and clearly explained a basic function for each.', '2026-06-25 15:05:37', '2026-06-25 15:03:53', '2026-06-25 15:05:37'),
(131, 34, 47, 3, 'weak_topic', 'To stay safe: Adults know how to block bad websites, close unsafe pop-ups, or report cyberbullies to keep you protected.To stop you from feeling worried: Talking to a trusted adult helps you understand what you saw and removes the feeling of fear or confusion.One example of private information you should never share online:Your home address', 1, 4.00, NULL, 'Excellent work! You clearly explained why it\'s important to ask an adult for help and gave a perfect example of private information.', '2026-06-25 15:05:59', '2026-06-25 15:03:53', '2026-06-25 15:05:59'),
(132, 34, 49, 4, 'weak_topic', 'Steps to Open the Program (2 marks)Click the Start button: Use your mouse to click the Start icon or search bar at the bottom-left corner of the screen.Select the drawing program: Type \"Paint\" or look through the app list, then click on the program icon to open it.Steps to Close the Program (2 marks)Save your work: Click on \"File\" and select \"Save\" so you do not lose your drawing.Click the \'X\' button: Move your mouse cursor to the top-right corner of the window and click the red cross (X) button to close iz.', NULL, NULL, 'teacher_review_required', NULL, '2026-06-25 15:06:37', '2026-06-25 15:03:53', '2026-06-25 15:06:37'),
(133, 34, 48, 5, 'spaced_review', '1. To find them easily laterHaving a clear name helps you know exactly what is inside the file without needing to open it.2. To avoid losing your work (Overwriting)Giving them different names prevents you from accidentally saving the dog story over the cat drawing, which would delete your hard work.3. To stay organizedIt keeps your computer computer folder neat so you can quickly tell the difference between your art files and your writing files', NULL, NULL, 'teacher_review_required', NULL, '2026-06-25 15:07:05', '2026-06-25 15:03:53', '2026-06-25 15:07:05'),
