(41, 4, 4, '12', 'The line joining the points A(3, q) and B(5-q, 8) has a gradient of 2. Calculate the value of q.', 4, 2, 2, 0.980, 'pending_review', NULL, '{\"extraction_method\":\"ai\",\"formulas\":[\"A(3, q)\",\"B(5-q, 8)\",\"gradient = 2\"],\"tables\":[],\"diagram_descriptions\":[],\"graph_descriptions\":[],\"subparts\":[],\"formula_count\":3,\"has_diagram\":false,\"has_graph\":false,\"has_table\":false,\"command_word\":\"calculate\",\"source_pages\":[2]}', NULL, NULL, '2026-07-04 12:46:24', '2026-07-04 12:46:24'),
(42, 4, 4, '13', 'Given that x varies jointly as y and inversely as the square of z, Calculate the missing value in Table 1.', 4, 2, 2, 0.980, 'pending_review', NULL, '{\"extraction_method\":\"ai\",\"formulas\":[\"x varies jointly as y and inversely as the square of z\"],\"tables\":[\"Table 1: | x | y | z | |---|---|---| | 3 | 1 | 2 | | ? | 3 | 6 |\"],\"diagram_descriptions\":[],\"graph_descriptions\":[],\"subparts\":[],\"formula_count\":1,\"has_diagram\":false,\"has_graph\":false,\"has_table\":true,\"command_word\":\"calculate\",\"source_pages\":[2]}', NULL, NULL, '2026-07-04 12:46:24', '2026-07-04 12:46:24'),
(43, 4, 4, '14', 'A box contains 5 red balls, 8 white balls and 7 black balls. If one ball is selected at random, Calculate the probability that the ball is white or black.', 5, 3, 3, 0.980, 'pending_review', NULL, '{\"extraction_method\":\"ai\",\"formulas\":[],\"tables\":[],\"diagram_descriptions\":[],\"graph_descriptions\":[],\"subparts\":[],\"formula_count\":0,\"has_diagram\":false,\"has_graph\":false,\"has_table\":false,\"command_word\":\"calculate\",\"source_pages\":[3]}', NULL, NULL, '2026-07-04 12:46:24', '2026-07-04 12:46:24'),
(44, 4, 4, '15', 'Table 2 shows the number of employees in 43 factories in a town. Draw a histogram.', 4, 3, 3, 0.980, 'pending_review', NULL, '{\"extraction_method\":\"ai\",\"formulas\":[],\"tables\":[\"Table 2: | Number of Employees | 0-39 | 40-59 | 60-79 | 80-99 | | Number of Factories | 5 | 15 | 13 | 10 |\"],\"diagram_descriptions\":[],\"graph_descriptions\":[\"Histogram showing Number of Employees vs Number of Factories based on Table 2.\"],\"subparts\":[],\"formula_count\":0,\"has_diagram\":false,\"has_graph\":true,\"has_table\":true,\"command_word\":\"draw\",\"source_pages\":[3]}', NULL, NULL, '2026-07-04 12:46:24', '2026-07-04 12:46:24'),
(45, 4, 4, '16', 'A circle centre O has a tangent PA at a point A. AT is a chord such that angle TAP is acute. If angle TAP = 70 degrees, Calculate the value of angle OTA.', 5, 3, 3, 0.980, 'pending_review', NULL, '{\"extraction_method\":\"ai\",\"formulas\":[\"angle TAP = 70 degrees\"],\"tables\":[],\"diagram_descriptions\":[],\"graph_descriptions\":[],\"subparts\":[],\"formula_count\":1,\"has_diagram\":false,\"has_graph\":false,\"has_table\":false,\"command_word\":\"calculate\",\"source_pages\":[3]}', NULL, NULL, '2026-07-04 12:46:24', '2026-07-04 12:46:24'),
(46, 4, 4, '17', 'The first three terms of a geometric progression are X+1, X^2+1 and 2X+1. Calculate the value of x.', 5, 3, 3, 0.980, 'pending_review', NULL, '{\"extraction_method\":\"ai\",\"formulas\":[\"X+1\",\"X^2+1\",\"2X+1\"],\"tables\":[],\"diagram_descriptions\":[],\"graph_descriptions\":[],\"subparts\":[],\"formula_count\":3,\"has_diagram\":false,\"has_graph\":false,\"has_table\":false,\"command_word\":\"calculate\",\"source_pages\":[3]}', NULL, NULL, '2026-07-04 12:46:24', '2026-07-04 12:46:24'),
(47, 4, 4, '18', 'P is a set of points (x, y) such that x > -1, y > -2 and y < 2 - x. Using a scale of 2 cm to represent 1 unit on both axes, show by shading the region which satisfies these inequalities.', 5, 3, 3, 0.980, 'pending_review', NULL, '{\"extraction_method\":\"ai\",\"formulas\":[\"x > -1\",\"y > -2\",\"y < 2 - x\"],\"tables\":[],\"diagram_descriptions\":[],\"graph_descriptions\":[\"Region defined by inequalities x > -1, y > -2, and y < 2 - x, to be shown by shading on a graph with a scale of 2 cm to 1 unit on both axes.\"],\"subparts\":[],\"formula_count\":3,\"has_diagram\":false,\"has_graph\":true,\"has_table\":false,\"command_word\":\"show\",\"source_pages\":[3]}', NULL, NULL, '2026-07-04 12:46:24', '2026-07-04 12:46:24'),
(48, 4, 4, '19', 'Figure 1 shows a speed-time graph for a particle during the first 20 seconds of its motion. Calculate the particle\'s average speed during the 20 seconds.', 5, 3, 3, 0.980, 'pending_review', NULL, '{\"extraction_method\":\"ai\",\"formulas\":[],\"tables\":[],\"diagram_descriptions\":[],\"graph_descriptions\":[\"Figure 1: A speed-time graph. X-axis: Time in seconds (0 to 20). Y-axis: Speed (m/s). The graph shows a line segment from (0, 0) to (10, 10) and then a horizontal line segment from (10, 10) to (20, 10).\"],\"subparts\":[],\"formula_count\":0,\"has_diagram\":false,\"has_graph\":true,\"has_table\":false,\"command_word\":\"calculate\",\"source_pages\":[3]}', NULL, NULL, '2026-07-04 12:46:24', '2026-07-04 12:46:24'),
(49, 4, 4, '20', 'A chord of a circle of radius 5 cm is 8 cm long. Sketch the diagram and calculate the angle subtended by the chord at the centre of the circle.', 6, 3, 3, 0.980, 'pending_review', NULL, '{\"extraction_method\":\"ai\",\"formulas\":[\"radius = 5 cm\",\"chord length = 8 cm\"],\"tables\":[],\"diagram_descriptions\":[\"A circle with radius 5 cm and a chord of length 8 cm. The diagram should show the center of the circle and the angle subtended by the chord at the center.\"],\"graph_descriptions\":[],\"subparts\":[],\"formula_count\":2,\"has_diagram\":true,\"has_graph\":false,\"has_table\":false,\"command_word\":\"calculate\",\"source_pages\":[3]}', NULL, NULL, '2026-07-04 12:46:24', '2026-07-04 12:46:24'),
(50, 4, 4, '21', 'Figure 2 shows a rectangular box with an open top. The box measures 6 cm long, x cm wide and x cm high. Given that the total outer surface area of the box is 108 cm^2. Form an equation in x and show that it simplifies to x^2 + 6x - 27 = 0.', 5, 4, 4, 0.980, 'pending_review', NULL, '{\"extraction_method\":\"ai\",\"formulas\":[\"length = 6 cm\",\"width = x cm\",\"height = x cm\",\"total outer surface area = 108 cm^2\",\"x^2 + 6x - 27 = 0\"],\"tables\":[],\"diagram_descriptions\":[\"Figure 2: A rectangular box with an open top. Dimensions are 6 cm (length), x cm (width), and x cm (height).\"],\"graph_descriptions\":[],\"subparts\":[],\"formula_count\":5,\"has_diagram\":true,\"has_graph\":false,\"has_table\":false,\"command_word\":\"form\",\"source_pages\":[4]}', NULL, NULL, '2026-07-04 12:46:24', '2026-07-04 12:46:24'),
(51, 4, 4, '22', 'In Figure 3, ABCD is a trapezium in which AB is parallel to DC. The diagonals AC and BD intersect at O such that OD = OC. Prove that the points A, B, C and D are concyclic.', 4, 4, 4, 0.980, 'pending_review', NULL, '{\"extraction_method\":\"ai\",\"formulas\":[\"AB is parallel to DC\",\"OD = OC\"],\"tables\":[],\"diagram_descriptions\":[\"Figure 3: A trapezium ABCD with AB parallel to DC. Diagonals AC and BD intersect at point O. OD = OC is indicated.\"],\"graph_descriptions\":[],\"subparts\":[],\"formula_count\":2,\"has_diagram\":true,\"has_graph\":false,\"has_table\":false,\"command_word\":\"prove\",\"source_pages\":[4]}', NULL, NULL, '2026-07-04 12:46:24', '2026-07-04 12:46:24'),
(52, 4, 4, '23', 'Find the remainder when 2x^3 - 13x + 12 is divided by 2x - 1.', 4, 4, 4, 0.980, 'pending_review', NULL, '{\"extraction_method\":\"ai\",\"formulas\":[\"2x^3 - 13x + 12\",\"2x - 1\"],\"tables\":[],\"diagram_descriptions\":[],\"graph_descriptions\":[],\"subparts\":[],\"formula_count\":2,\"has_diagram\":false,\"has_graph\":false,\"has_table\":false,\"command_word\":\"find\",\"source_pages\":[4]}', NULL, NULL, '2026-07-04 12:46:24', '2026-07-04 12:46:24'),
(53, 4, 4, '24', 'Draw a circle centre O with radius 3 cm. Construct another circle radius 4 cm passing through point O. Label its centre C. Label one of the intersection points of the two circles A. Using a ruler only, Construct a tangent to the circle centre O at point A. Measure and state angle AOC.', 5, 4, 4, 0.980, 'pending_review', NULL, '{\"extraction_method\":\"ai\",\"formulas\":[\"radius of first circle = 3 cm\",\"radius of second circle = 4 cm\"],\"tables\":[],\"diagram_descriptions\":[\"Construction of two circles: one with centre O and radius 3 cm, another with centre C and radius 4 cm passing through O. Point A is an intersection of the two circles. A tangent to the circle centre O at point A needs to be constructed. Angle AOC needs to be measured.\"],\"graph_descriptions\":[],\"subparts\":[],\"formula_count\":2,\"has_diagram\":true,\"has_graph\":false,\"has_table\":false,\"command_word\":\"construct\",\"source_pages\":[4]}', NULL, NULL, '2026-07-04 12:46:24', '2026-07-04 12:46:24');
