(60, 1, 9, 37, 27, 201, NULL, 'multiple_choice', 'What is an effect of littering in our community?', '[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Making places look beautiful\"},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Helping plants grow better\"},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"Making places look dirty and untidy\"},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"Attracting more visitors\"}]', 'C', '[]', 'Littering makes our environment dirty and untidy, which can also harm animals and the environment.', 'Not understanding the negative consequences of littering.', 'easy', 'identify', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 32, 32, '2026-06-21 08:29:24', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-21 08:26:18', '2026-06-21 08:29:24', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(61, 1, 9, 37, 27, 201, NULL, 'short_answer', 'Describe one negative effect of wasting resources like paper or electricity.', '[]', 'Accept answers such as: It harms the environment; It means we might run out of resources; It costs more money; It creates more waste.', '[\"It harms the environment\",\"It means we might run out of resources\",\"It costs more money\",\"It creates more waste\"]', 'Wasting resources can lead to environmental damage, depletion of natural materials, and increased costs.', 'Focusing only on personal inconvenience rather than broader environmental or economic impacts.', 'easy', 'describe', 2, 0.850, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 32, 32, '2026-06-21 08:29:25', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-21 08:26:18', '2026-06-21 08:29:25', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(62, 1, 9, 37, 27, 201, NULL, 'multiple_choice', 'If a map shows a small blue rectangle, what might it represent?', '[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"A mountain\"},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"A lake or pond\"},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"A road\"},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"A school\"}]', 'B', '[]', 'Blue is commonly used on maps to represent water bodies like lakes, rivers, or ponds. A small rectangle could indicate a small body of water.', 'Not associating colors with common geographical features on maps.', 'easy', 'identify', 1, 0.800, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 32, 32, '2026-06-21 08:29:25', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-21 08:26:18', '2026-06-21 08:29:25', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(63, 1, 9, 37, 27, 201, NULL, 'structured', 'Imagine you are drawing a simple map of your bedroom. Draw a simple symbol for your bed and label it. Then, draw a symbol for your door and label it.', '[]', 'A simple drawing of a bed (e.g., a rectangle with a pillow shape) labeled \'Bed\'. A simple drawing of a door (e.g., a rectangle with a small circle for a handle) labeled \'Door\'.', '[]', 'Map symbols are simplified drawings that represent real-world objects. Labeling helps others understand what the symbols mean.', 'Drawing too much detail or forgetting to label the symbols.', 'easy', 'draw', 4, 0.850, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 32, 32, '2026-06-21 08:29:26', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-21 08:26:18', '2026-06-21 08:29:26', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(64, 1, 9, 37, 27, 201, NULL, 'multiple_choice', 'Why might you wear a warm jacket and hat on a very cold and windy day?', '[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"To look fashionable\"},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"To stay warm and protect yourself from the cold\"},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"To make it harder to run\"},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"To carry more things\"}]', 'B', '[]', 'Clothing choices are often made to suit the weather. Warm jackets and hats help keep us warm and protected when it\'s cold and windy.', 'Not connecting clothing directly to weather conditions and personal comfort/safety.', 'easy', 'explain', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 32, 32, '2026-06-21 08:29:26', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-21 08:26:18', '2026-06-21 08:29:26', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(65, 1, 9, 37, 27, 201, NULL, 'short_answer', 'Compare the type of clothing you would wear on a sunny day versus a rainy day.', '[]', 'On a sunny day, you would wear light clothes like a t-shirt and shorts. On a rainy day, you would wear a raincoat, boots, and maybe carry an umbrella.', '[\"Sunny: light clothes, t-shirt, shorts. Rainy: raincoat, boots, umbrella.\"]', 'Different weather conditions require different clothing to keep us comfortable and protected. Sunny weather calls for light clothing, while rainy weather requires waterproof gear.', 'Only describing one type of weather or not making a clear comparison.', 'easy', 'compare', 2, 0.850, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 32, 32, '2026-06-21 08:29:27', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-21 08:26:18', '2026-06-21 08:29:27', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(66, 1, 9, 37, 27, 201, NULL, 'multiple_choice', 'What is a \'natural feature\'?', '[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Something built by people\"},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Something found in nature, not made by people\"},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"A type of animal\"},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"A drawing on a map\"}]', 'B', '[]', 'Natural features are parts of the Earth\'s landscape that were formed by natural processes, such as mountains, rivers, and forests.', 'Confusing the definition with human-made features.', 'easy', 'define', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 32, 32, '2026-06-21 08:29:28', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-21 08:26:18', '2026-06-21 08:29:28', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(67, 1, 9, 37, 27, 201, NULL, 'short_answer', 'List two ways you can help keep your local park clean and tidy.', '[]', 'Accept any two valid ways such as: Put rubbish in the bins; Don\'t pick flowers; Don\'t damage plants; Report broken equipment; Clean up after pets.', '[\"Put rubbish in the bins\",\"Don\'t pick flowers\",\"Don\'t damage plants\",\"Report broken equipment\",\"Clean up after pets\"]', 'Caring for public spaces like parks ensures they remain pleasant and safe for everyone to enjoy.', 'Listing only one way or providing a general answer without specific actions.', 'easy', 'list', 2, 0.850, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 32, 32, '2026-06-21 08:29:28', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-21 08:26:18', '2026-06-21 08:29:28', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(68, 1, 9, 37, 27, 201, NULL, 'multiple_choice', 'If the library is \'north\' of your classroom, and the playground is \'east\' of the library, where is the playground relative to your classroom?', '[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"North-east\"},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"South-west\"},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"North-west\"},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"South-east\"}]', 'A', '[]', 'If the library is north, and the playground is east of the library, then from the classroom, the playground would be in the north-east direction.', 'Getting confused with compound directions or relative positioning.', 'easy', 'use', 1, 0.800, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 32, 32, '2026-06-21 08:29:29', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-21 08:26:18', '2026-06-21 08:29:29', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(69, 1, 9, 37, 27, 201, NULL, 'structured', 'Imagine you are a weather reporter for your school. For tomorrow, predict the weather using simple terms (e.g., sunny, cloudy, rainy, windy) and explain what you would advise students to wear.', '[]', 'Accept a clear weather prediction (e.g., \'Tomorrow will be sunny and warm.\') and appropriate clothing advice (e.g., \'Wear light clothes like t-shirts and shorts, and don\'t forget your hats!\').', '[]', 'Weather observations help us predict future conditions and make practical decisions, such as choosing appropriate clothing.', 'Not providing both a weather description and clothing advice, or giving advice that doesn\'t match the predicted weather.', 'easy', 'explain', 3, 0.850, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 32, 32, '2026-06-21 08:29:29', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-21 08:26:18', '2026-06-21 08:29:29', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(70, 1, 9, 37, 4, 173, NULL, 'structured', 'A scientist wants to find out if different types of soil affect how tall a plant grows. She plans to plant three identical seeds in three different pots, each with a different type of soil (sandy, clay, and loam). She will give them the same amount of water every day and keep them in the same sunny spot.a) What is the one thing the scientist is changing in this investigation?b) List two things the scientist is keeping the same to make it a fair test.c) Why is it important to keep other things the same?', '[]', 'a) The type of soil.b) Any two from: amount of water, type of seed, amount of sunlight/location, size of pot.c) To make sure that any difference in plant height is only because of the soil type, and not because of other factors. If other things changed, she wouldn\'t know what caused the difference.', '[]', 'In a fair test, only one variable should be changed at a time to ensure that any observed results are directly caused by that specific change. All other conditions must be kept constant to prevent them from influencing the outcome, allowing for a clear cause-and-effect relationship to be identified.', 'Students might struggle to identify the single changing variable or list things that are not relevant to the experiment\'s fairness. Some might also not fully explain *why* keeping things the same is important, just stating that it \'makes it fair\'.', 'hard', 'Planning, Identifying variables, Explaining scientific principles', 4, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 38, 38, '2026-06-21 22:13:01', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-21 22:10:42', '2026-06-25 14:58:49', NULL, 3, 25.00, 0, NULL),
(71, 1, 9, 37, 4, 173, NULL, 'multiple_choice', 'Why is it important for people to use natural resources like water and trees responsibly?', '[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"So that we have enough resources for ourselves right now.\"},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"So that there will be enough resources for future generations.\"},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"So that we can sell them for more money later.\"},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"So that animals have more places to live.\"}]', 'B', '[\"B\"]', 'Responsible use of natural resources ensures that they are not depleted, allowing future generations to also benefit from them. This concept is known as sustainability, which is about meeting our own needs without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their own needs.', 'Students might choose options that focus on immediate benefits (A) or specific environmental aspects (D) rather than the broader, long-term goal of sustainability for future generations.', 'hard', 'Explaining, Understanding consequences', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 38, 38, '2026-06-21 22:13:14', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-21 22:10:42', '2026-06-25 14:56:58', NULL, 5, 66.67, 0, NULL),
(72, 1, 9, 37, 4, 173, NULL, 'short_answer', 'Describe two clear differences you would observe in the sky during the day compared to the night.', '[]', '1. During the day, the sun is visible and the sky is bright, while at night, the sun is not visible and the sky is dark.2. During the day, we often see clouds, while at night we can often see the moon and stars (if not cloudy). (Accept any two distinct and accurate observable differences in the sky.)', '[]', 'The Earth\'s rotation causes different parts of the planet to face the sun, resulting in day and night. This rotation leads to distinct observable features in the sky, such as the presence of the sun and brightness during the day, and the moon and stars against a dark sky at night.', 'Students might give very general answers like \'day is bright, night is dark\' without mentioning specific celestial bodies or observable features. They might also describe activities instead of features of the sky.', 'hard', 'Comparing, Describing observations', 2, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 38, 38, '2026-06-21 22:13:21', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-21 22:10:42', '2026-06-25 14:58:03', NULL, 3, 50.00, 0, NULL),
(73, 1, 9, 37, 4, 173, NULL, 'structured', 'Imagine you have two different types of paper towels, and you want to find out which one absorbs more water.a) Write one scientific question you could ask about this.b) Describe how you would observe and record your findings to answer your question. (Hint: Think about what you would look for and how you would write it down.)', '[]', 'a) Which type of paper towel absorbs the most water? / Does Brand A or Brand B paper towel absorb more water? / How much water can different paper towels absorb? (Any clear, testable scientific question related to absorbency).b) I would pour the same amount of water onto each paper towel (e.g., 10ml). I would then observe how much water is left or how much water each paper towel soaked up. I could record this by measuring the remaining water in a cup or by weighing the paper towels before and after soaking. I could use a table to write down the results for each paper towel type.', '[]', 'A scientific question needs to be testable and specific. When observing and recording, it\'s important to have a clear method for measurement and a structured way to document the results, such as a table, to make comparisons easy and reliable.', 'Students might ask a non-scientific question (e.g., \'Which paper towel is better?\') or describe an observation without a clear method for measuring/recording the amount of water absorbed.', 'hard', 'Asking scientific questions, Planning observations, Recording data', 3, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 38, 38, '2026-06-21 22:13:35', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-21 22:10:42', '2026-06-25 14:59:50', NULL, 3, 0.00, 0, NULL),
(74, 1, 9, 37, 4, 173, NULL, 'multiple_choice', 'Which statement best explains what a \'fair test\' means in science?', '[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"It means everyone gets a turn to do the experiment.\"},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"It means you only change one thing at a time to see its effect.\"},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"It means you always get the answer you expect.\"},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"It means you use the most expensive equipment.\"}]', 'B', '[\"B\"]', 'A fair test is crucial in science to ensure that any observed changes are due to the specific variable being tested, and not other factors. By changing only one thing (the independent variable) and keeping all other conditions the same (controlled variables), scientists can confidently conclude the cause-and-effect relationship.', 'Students might confuse \'fair\' with everyday fairness (like taking turns) or think it means getting a desired outcome. They may not grasp the concept of isolating a single variable.', 'hard', 'Defining, Explaining concepts', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 38, 38, '2026-06-21 22:13:49', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-21 22:10:42', '2026-06-25 14:59:31', NULL, 3, 75.00, 0, NULL),
(75, 1, 9, 37, 2, 187, NULL, 'multiple_choice', 'What is the value of the digit \'7\' in the number 375?', '[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"7\"},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"70\"},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"700\"}]', 'B', '[\"70\",\"seventy\"]', 'In the number 375, the digit \'7\' is in the tens place. This means its value is 7 tens, which is 70.', 'Students might confuse the digit itself with its place value, answering \'7\' instead of \'70\'.', 'easy', 'identify', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 38, 38, '2026-06-22 06:25:50', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-22 06:25:10', '2026-06-22 06:25:50', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(76, 1, 9, 37, 2, 187, NULL, 'short_answer', 'Calculate: 245 + 132 =', '[]', '377', '[\"377\"]', 'To solve 245 + 132, you can add the ones (5+2=7), then the tens (40+30=70), then the hundreds (200+100=300). Adding these together: 300 + 70 + 7 = 377.', 'Students might make errors in carrying over or aligning digits incorrectly if using a written method.', 'easy', 'calculate', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 38, 38, '2026-06-22 06:26:04', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-22 06:25:11', '2026-06-22 06:26:04', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(77, 1, 9, 37, 2, 187, NULL, 'multiple_choice', 'Which unit would you most likely use to measure the length of a classroom?', '[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Centimetres\"},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Metres\"},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"Millilitres\"}]', 'B', '[\"Metres\",\"meters\"]', 'Centimetres are too small for a classroom. Millilitres measure capacity, not length. Metres are a sensible unit for measuring the length of larger objects like a classroom.', 'Students might choose a unit that is too small (centimetres) or confuse units of length with units of capacity.', 'easy', 'select', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 38, 38, '2026-06-22 06:26:10', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-22 06:25:11', '2026-06-22 06:26:10', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(78, 1, 9, 37, 2, 187, NULL, 'short_answer', 'How many straight sides does a triangle have?', '[]', '3', '[\"3\",\"three\"]', 'A triangle is a 2D shape defined by having three straight sides and three vertices (corners).', 'Students might confuse the number of sides with the number of corners, or with other shapes.', 'easy', 'identify', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 38, 38, '2026-06-22 06:26:22', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-22 06:25:11', '2026-06-22 06:26:22', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(79, 1, 9, 37, 2, 187, NULL, 'structured', 'Order these numbers from smallest to largest: 512, 215, 152.', '[]', '152, 215, 512', '[\"152, 215, 512\"]', 'To order numbers, compare their hundreds digit first. 152 has 1 hundred, 215 has 2 hundreds, and 512 has 5 hundreds. So, 152 is the smallest, followed by 215, and then 512.', 'Students might order them from largest to smallest, or make errors when comparing digits if the hundreds digits were the same.', 'easy', 'order', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 38, 38, '2026-06-22 06:26:29', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-06-22 06:25:11', '2026-06-22 06:26:29', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(80, 3, 16, 76, 65, 315, NULL, 'multiple_choice', 'Which of these is a reason why trees are important?', '[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"They make the air dirty.\"},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"They give us shade.\"},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"They make loud noises.\"}]', 'B', '[\"B\"]', 'Trees are important because they provide shade, which helps keep us cool. They also give us fruits, clean the air, and provide homes for animals.', 'Some learners might confuse the benefits of trees with negative aspects, or pick an irrelevant option.', 'easy', 'Identify', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 137, 137, '2026-07-02 09:14:16', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-07-02 09:13:39', '2026-07-02 21:28:36', NULL, 2, 66.67, 0, NULL),
(81, 3, 16, 76, 65, 315, NULL, 'short_answer', 'Name one bad thing that happens when too many trees are cut down.', '[]', 'When too many trees are cut down, animals lose their homes, the soil can be washed away easily (soil erosion), and the air can become less clean.', '[\"Animals lose homes\",\"Soil gets washed away\",\"Air becomes less clean\",\"It gets hotter\"]', 'Trees provide homes for many animals and help hold the soil in place. When they are cut down, animals lose their habitats, and the soil can be eroded by wind and rain. Trees also help keep the air clean.', 'Learners might struggle to articulate a specific bad effect, or give a very general answer like \'it\'s bad\'.', 'easy', 'Recall', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 137, 137, '2026-07-02 09:14:11', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-07-02 09:13:40', '2026-07-02 21:28:51', NULL, 2, 66.67, 0, NULL),
(82, 3, 16, 76, 65, 315, NULL, 'multiple_choice', 'Why are bush fires harmful to the environment?', '[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"They help new plants grow faster.\"},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"They destroy homes for animals.\"},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"They make the air smell nice.\"}]', 'B', '[\"B\"]', 'Bush fires burn down plants and trees, which destroys the places where animals live. They also kill animals and make the air smoky and unhealthy.', 'Some learners might think fires are natural and therefore not harmful, or confuse them with controlled burns for agriculture.', 'easy', 'Identify', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 137, 137, '2026-07-02 09:14:13', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-07-02 09:13:40', '2026-07-02 21:28:52', NULL, 2, 66.67, 0, NULL),
(83, 3, 16, 76, 65, 315, NULL, 'structured', 'Describe one simple way you can help keep a river or well clean in your community.', '[]', 'One way to keep a river or well clean is to avoid throwing rubbish or waste into it. We should also make sure that dirty water from washing or bathing does not flow directly into the water source.', '[\"Do not throw rubbish in the water\",\"Do not wash clothes near the water source\",\"Do not let animals drink directly from the well\",\"Clean up rubbish near the water source\"]', 'Keeping water sources clean is very important for everyone\'s health. Simple actions like not littering near or in the water, and preventing dirty water from entering, can make a big difference.', 'Learners might give a very vague answer or suggest something impractical for their age. They might also focus on general cleanliness rather than water-specific actions.', 'easy', 'Describe', 2, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 137, 137, '2026-07-02 09:14:14', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-07-02 09:13:40', '2026-07-02 09:18:20', NULL, 2, 0.00, 0, NULL),
(84, 3, 16, 76, 65, 315, NULL, 'short_answer', 'What is one thing you can do to protect the environment around your school or home?', '[]', 'One thing I can do is to put rubbish in the bin, plant a tree, or save water.', '[\"Put rubbish in the bin\",\"Plant a tree\",\"Save water\",\"Do not cut down trees\",\"Clean up litter\"]', 'Protecting our environment means taking care of the land, water, and air around us. Simple actions like proper waste disposal, planting trees, and conserving water all help.', 'Learners might struggle to think of a specific, actionable item, or give an answer that is too broad.', 'easy', 'Identify', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 137, 137, '2026-07-02 09:14:15', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-07-02 09:13:40', '2026-07-02 21:29:13', NULL, 2, 66.67, 0, NULL);
INSERT INTO `question_bank` (`id`, `school_id`, `curriculum_id`, `grade_id`, `subject_id`, `topic_id`, `subtopic_id`, `question_type`, `question_text`, `options_json`, `correct_answer`, `accepted_answers_json`, `explanation`, `common_mistake`, `difficulty`, `skill_type`, `marks`, `confidence`, `source_type`, `approval_status`, `created_by`, `approved_by`, `approved_at`, `ai_model_used`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `quality_score`, `times_attempted`, `percent_correct`, `flag_count`, `last_reviewed_at`) VALUES
(85, 3, 16, 76, 65, 312, NULL, 'multiple_choice', 'Which tool is used for digging holes and weeding in the garden?', '[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Rake\"},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Hoe\"},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"Watering can\"},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"Wheelbarrow\"}]', 'B', '[\"B\",\"Hoe\"]', 'A hoe is a common farm tool specifically designed for digging, cultivating soil, and removing weeds. A rake is for gathering, a watering can for watering, and a wheelbarrow for transporting.', 'Confusing the hoe with a rake, as both are used in soil, but for different primary tasks.', 'easy', 'identify', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 137, 137, '2026-07-02 12:10:28', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-07-02 12:09:39', '2026-07-02 12:10:28', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(86, 3, 16, 76, 65, 312, NULL, 'short_answer', 'Name one tool you would use to water your plants in the garden.', '[]', 'Watering can', '[\"Watering can\",\"Hose\",\"Bucket\"]', 'A watering can is a common and essential tool for providing water to plants, especially in a small garden. A hose or bucket can also be used.', 'Naming a tool not used for watering, such as a hoe or rake.', 'easy', 'name', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 137, 137, '2026-07-02 12:10:41', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-07-02 12:09:39', '2026-07-02 12:10:41', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(87, 3, 16, 76, 65, 312, NULL, 'structured', 'Explain what a rake is primarily used for in the garden.', '[]', 'A rake is primarily used for gathering leaves, smoothing soil, or collecting small stones and debris from the garden bed.', '[\"To gather leaves\",\"To smooth soil\",\"To collect small stones\",\"To remove debris\"]', 'Rakes have teeth that are effective for sweeping and leveling surfaces, making them ideal for clearing garden beds or preparing soil.', 'Describing the use of a hoe (digging) instead of a rake (gathering/smoothing).', 'easy', 'explain', 2, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 137, 137, '2026-07-02 12:10:57', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-07-02 12:09:39', '2026-07-02 12:10:57', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(88, 3, 16, 76, 65, 312, NULL, 'multiple_choice', 'What is the most important thing to do with farm tools after you finish using them?', '[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Leave them on the ground where you used them\"},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Put them away safely in their proper place\"},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"Play with them with your friends\"},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"Hide them so no one else can use them\"}]', 'B', '[\"B\",\"Put them away safely in their proper place\"]', 'Putting tools away safely prevents accidents, keeps the garden tidy, and helps to preserve the tools for future use.', 'Leaving tools lying around, which can cause trips or injuries.', 'easy', 'list', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 137, 137, '2026-07-02 12:46:24', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-07-02 12:09:39', '2026-07-02 12:46:24', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(89, 3, 16, 76, 65, 312, NULL, 'short_answer', 'Why is it important to wash your hands thoroughly after working in the garden?', '[]', 'It is important to wash your hands to remove dirt, germs, and any harmful substances from the soil that could make you sick.', '[\"To remove dirt\",\"To remove germs\",\"To prevent getting sick\",\"To be clean\"]', 'Soil can contain bacteria and other microorganisms. Washing hands helps maintain hygiene and prevents the spread of illness.', 'Not understanding the health implications and only mentioning \'to be clean\'.', 'easy', 'explain', 2, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 137, 137, '2026-07-02 12:46:27', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-07-02 12:09:39', '2026-07-02 12:46:27', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(90, 3, 16, 76, 65, 312, NULL, 'multiple_choice', 'When holding a hoe to dig, where should your hands be placed for the best control and safety?', '[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Both hands at the very top of the handle\"},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Both hands at the very bottom of the handle\"},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"One hand near the top and one hand lower down on the handle\"},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"Only one hand on the handle\"}]', 'C', '[\"C\",\"One hand near the top and one hand lower down on the handle\"]', 'Holding a hoe with one hand near the top and the other lower down provides better leverage, control, and balance, making it safer and more effective for digging.', 'Holding the hoe with hands too close together or too far apart, reducing control.', 'easy', 'demonstrate', 1, 0.800, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 137, 137, '2026-07-02 12:46:28', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-07-02 12:09:39', '2026-07-02 12:46:28', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(91, 3, 16, 76, 65, 312, NULL, 'short_answer', 'How should you carry a sharp garden tool, like a hoe or a spade, to ensure safety?', '[]', 'You should carry it with the sharp part pointing down towards the ground, or carry it over your shoulder with the sharp part behind you.', '[\"Sharp part pointing down\",\"Over shoulder with sharp part behind\",\"Pointed away from others\"]', 'Carrying sharp tools with the blade pointing downwards or behind you prevents accidental cuts to yourself or others, especially if you trip.', 'Carrying the tool carelessly, with the sharp part pointing upwards or forwards.', 'easy', 'demonstrate', 2, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 137, 137, '2026-07-02 12:46:30', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-07-02 12:09:39', '2026-07-02 12:46:30', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(92, 3, 16, 76, 65, 312, NULL, 'structured', 'Name two different farm tools and for each tool, state one safety rule you should follow when using it.', '[]', '1. Hoe: Always carry it with the sharp blade pointing down towards the ground. 2. Rake: Do not leave it lying on the ground with the teeth facing upwards.', '[\"Hoe: Carry with blade down.\",\"Rake: Don\'t leave teeth up.\",\"Watering can: Don\'t run when full.\",\"Spade: Don\'t swing it carelessly.\"]', 'Following safety rules for each tool prevents common accidents. For a hoe, the sharp blade can cause injury if not carried correctly. For a rake, upward-facing teeth can cause someone to trip or step on them.', 'Naming tools but not providing a specific safety rule, or providing a general safety rule not specific to the tool.', 'easy', 'list', 4, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 137, 137, '2026-07-02 12:46:32', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-07-02 12:09:39', '2026-07-02 12:46:32', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(93, 3, 16, 76, 65, 312, NULL, 'multiple_choice', 'Which tool has long, comb-like teeth and is used to gather leaves or smooth soil?', '[{\"label\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Spade\"},{\"label\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Hoe\"},{\"label\":\"C\",\"text\":\"Rake\"},{\"label\":\"D\",\"text\":\"Trowel\"}]', 'C', '[\"C\",\"Rake\"]', 'The description perfectly matches a rake, which is designed with teeth to collect loose materials or level surfaces.', 'Confusing a rake with a hoe, which has a flat blade for digging.', 'easy', 'identify', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 137, 137, '2026-07-02 12:46:34', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-07-02 12:09:39', '2026-07-02 12:46:34', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL),
(94, 3, 16, 76, 65, 312, NULL, 'short_answer', 'Besides washing your hands, name one other important safety rule to follow after you have finished using farm tools.', '[]', 'Always put the tools away in their proper storage place.', '[\"Put tools away safely\",\"Clean tools before storing\",\"Do not leave tools lying around\"]', 'Storing tools correctly prevents them from being a tripping hazard, protects them from weather, and ensures they are easy to find next time.', 'Stating a safety rule for *during* use, rather than *after* use.', 'easy', 'list', 1, 0.900, 'ai_generated', 'approved', 137, 137, '2026-07-02 12:46:36', 'gemini-2.5-flash', '2026-07-02 12:09:39', '2026-07-02 12:46:36', NULL, 0, NULL, 0, NULL);
