(963, 12, 3, 'topic', NULL, 'Inequalities in living standards', 'This theme responds to two key aspects of the economic, political and ethical debate over global inequality in the last 25 years – debates which continue to be urgently relevant. The UN’s Millennium Development Goals identify inequalities in health and the consequences of those inequalities as a major factor in global injustice, and seek to make progress in tackling them by 2015. From the Live 8 response to G8 international debt agreement to continuing debates over aid and trade, broader inequalities of wealth and their consequences continue to be a major issue. This sequence of lessons provides some starting points for students to explore these problems and both gather and evaluate relevant evidence in order to increase their levels of knowledge. It then goes on to provide some structured sequences for debating and judging this evidence, and producing sustained academic arguments in written form.', '35', NULL, NULL, NULL, 0.950, 'approved', 137, '2026-07-02 13:02:41', 321, '{\"topic_name\":\"Inequalities in living standards\",\"description\":\"This theme responds to two key aspects of the economic, political and ethical debate over global inequality in the last 25 years – debates which continue to be urgently relevant. The UN’s Millennium Development Goals identify inequalities in health and the consequences of those inequalities as a major factor in global injustice, and seek to make progress in tackling them by 2015. From the Live 8 response to G8 international debt agreement to continuing debates over aid and trade, broader inequalities of wealth and their consequences continue to be a major issue. This sequence of lessons provides some starting points for students to explore these problems and both gather and evaluate relevant evidence in order to increase their levels of knowledge. It then goes on to provide some structured sequences for debating and judging this evidence, and producing sustained academic arguments in written form.\",\"confidence\":0.95,\"subtopics\":[{\"subtopic_name\":\"Introduction to the theme and the unit\",\"learning_objectives\":[\"Identify the overall content (theme areas) and assessment focus of this unit.\",\"Apply a checklist to conduct an audit of skills learnt at AS, including critical analysis of sources, research, writing, and presentational skills.\",\"Describe the results of the skills audit with peers and the class.\"],\"skills\":[\"identify\",\"apply\",\"describe\"],\"suggested_week\":null,\"exam_relevance\":\"low\",\"keywords\":[\"theme introduction\",\"unit overview\",\"assessment focus\",\"skills audit\",\"AS-level skills\",\"critical analysis\",\"research skills\",\"writing skills\",\"presentation skills\"],\"prerequisites\":[],\"confidence\":0.9},{\"subtopic_name\":\"Inequalities in health – what is happening?\",\"learning_objectives\":[\"Identify the context of the UN’s Millennium Development Goals by exploring the official website.\",\"Identify specific inequalities of health highlighted in the ‘Make it Happen’ (2008) video.\",\"Evaluate the credibility and reliability of sources, considering reputation, selectivity, and currency.\",\"Analyse data and context for child health (Goal 4), maternal health (Goal 5), and reducing HIV/AIDS (Goal 6) from UN resources.\",\"Describe findings on specific health goals to the class.\",\"Define health inequity based on the UN WHO factfile.\",\"Identify factors associated with the causes of health inequity from the UN WHO factfile.\"],\"skills\":[\"identify\",\"evaluate\",\"analyse\",\"describe\",\"define\"],\"suggested_week\":null,\"exam_relevance\":\"high\",\"keywords\":[\"health inequalities\",\"UN Millennium Development Goals\",\"child health\",\"maternal health\",\"HIV/AIDS\",\"source credibility\",\"source reliability\",\"health inequity definition\",\"causes of health inequity\"],\"prerequisites\":[\"Basic research skills\",\"Understanding of global issues\"],\"confidence\":0.95},{\"subtopic_name\":\"Why is this happening? Investigating the evidence base.\",\"learning_objectives\":[\"Analyse evidence on sanitation, clean water, adequate nutrition, and access to medicines using provided resources.\",\"Analyse and evaluate evidence in terms of credibility, reliability, relevance, and significance.\",\"Identify relevant evidence related to the causes of health inequality.\",\"Evaluate evidence to support understanding of health inequality causes.\",\"Apply identified evidence to possible causes of health inequality.\",\"Create a poster presentation identifying, evaluating, and linking evidence to health inequality causes.\"],\"skills\":[\"analyse\",\"evaluate\",\"identify\",\"apply\",\"create\"],\"suggested_week\":null,\"exam_relevance\":\"high\",\"keywords\":[\"sanitation\",\"clean water\",\"nutrition\",\"access to medicines\",\"evidence analysis\",\"credibility\",\"reliability\",\"relevance\",\"significance\",\"causes of health inequality\",\"poster presentation\"],\"prerequisites\":[\"Understanding of health inequalities\",\"Basic research and evaluation skills\"],\"confidence\":0.95},{\"subtopic_name\":\"What, if any, action needs to be taken? Analysing and evaluating contrasting arguments.\",\"learning_objectives\":[\"Analyse the argument structure of two opposing viewpoints on solutions to global health inequalities.\",\"Identify the two positions presented in contrasting arguments.\",\"Evaluate the strength of arguments based on previously explored evidence.\",\"Evaluate and explain personal judgments on the issue of global health inequalities.\",\"Explain the current situation of global health inequalities with relevant examples.\",\"Analyse the evidence for why global health inequalities are happening.\",\"Create and explain the best solution to global health inequalities.\"],\"skills\":[\"analyse\",\"identify\",\"evaluate\",\"explain\",\"create\"],\"suggested_week\":null,\"exam_relevance\":\"high\",\"keywords\":[\"global health inequalities solutions\",\"contrasting arguments\",\"argument analysis\",\"evidence-based judgment\",\"foreign aid\",\"development aid\",\"justification\",\"essay writing\"],\"prerequisites\":[\"Understanding of global health inequalities and their causes\",\"Ability to analyse and evaluate evidence\"],\"confidence\":0.95}]}', '2026-07-02 12:56:29', '2026-07-02 13:02:41'),
